                    <chunk name="param_input" index="8">
                      <items count="9">
                        <item name="Description" type_name="gh_string" type_code="10">Which half to run. Everything runs the WPS half, builds run_wrf/namelist.input from its output (WRF's own physics kept), then runs the WRF half. WPS output does not change unless the domains or the met data do, so re-running the WRF half alone is the normal edit-and-retry loop: it uses the namelist.input in run_wrf exactly as you left it (time step, physics, run length), and only builds one when there is none. Time Step and History Interval, when set, are the exception: they are written into that file.</item>
                        <item name="InstanceGuid" type_name="gh_guid" type_code="9">42d6f8f0-4736-4cf9-bc75-132cc029b79f</item>
