            <chunk name="Object" index="18">
              <items count="2">
                <item name="GUID" type_name="gh_guid" type_code="9">59e0b89a-e487-49f8-bab8-b5bab16be14c</item>
                <item name="Name" type_name="gh_string" type_code="10">Panel</item>
              </items>
              <chunks count="1">
                <chunk name="Container">
                  <items count="8">
                    <item name="Description" type_name="gh_string" type_code="10">A panel for custom notes and text values</item>
                    <item name="InstanceGuid" type_name="gh_guid" type_code="9">7728f24b-10ac-5cfa-997e-3e1f25103403</item>
                    <item name="Name" type_name="gh_string" type_code="10">Panel</item>
                    <item name="NickName" type_name="gh_string" type_code="10">Description</item>
                    <item name="Optional" type_name="gh_bool" type_code="1">false</item>
                    <item name="ScrollRatio" type_name="gh_double" type_code="6">0</item>
                    <item name="SourceCount" type_name="gh_int32" type_code="3">0</item>
                    <item name="UserText" type_name="gh_string" type_code="10">Purpose: Site weather for Atlanta from a regional WRF run driven by GFS forecasts.
Fidelity: Experimental - mesoscale workflow; 3 km nest on low-resolution geography.
Method: WRF Met Data fetches 0.25 degree GFS from NOMADS; 3 km Lambert nest inside a 9 km parent; WPS and WRF run in a container.
Result: 2 m temperature and 10 m wind viewers; WRF Weather and WRF ABL derive CFD weather and inflow.
Needs: Eddy3D Setup &gt; Mesoscale weather / Weather Research and Forecasting (WRF). Runtime: hours.
Edit: Dates (NOMADS keeps about ten days), domain centre and size.</item>
                  </items>
                  <chunks count="2">
                    <chunk name="Attributes">
                      <items count="5">
                        <item name="Bounds" type_name="gh_drawing_rectanglef" type_code="35">
